\fs32\b Workflows & Best Practices\b0\fs22\par\par
\par
\fs28\b Story Development Workflow\b0\fs22\par
\par
\tab 1. **Product Manager Creates Story**\par
   - Write clear title and description\par
   - Define acceptance criteria\par
   - Set priority and story points\par
   - Add to sprint (optional)\par
\par
\tab 2. **QA Engineer Reviews**\par
   - Verify acceptance criteria are testable\par
   - Request clarifications if needed\par
   - Provide QA Sign-Off when satisfied\par
\par
\tab 3. **Product Manager Approves**\par
   - Review finalized story\par
   - Provide PM Approval\par
   - Story unlocks for development\par
\par
\tab 4. **Assignments Made**\par
   - Assign developer\par
   - Assign tester\par
   - Set due dates\par
\par
\tab 5. **Development**\par
   - Developer implements feature\par
   - Updates story status\par
   - Links commits/PRs\par
\par
\tab 6. **Testing**\par
   - Tester executes test cases\par
   - Reports bugs if found\par
   - Validates acceptance criteria\par
\par
\tab 7. **Completion**\par
   - All tests pass\par
   - No open bugs\par
   - Story marked "Done"\par
\par
\fs28\b Test Case Creation Workflow\b0\fs22\par
\par
\tab 1. **Review Story**\par
   - Read acceptance criteria\par
   - Understand requirements\par
   - Identify test scenarios\par
\par
\tab 2. **Create Test Case**\par
   - Write descriptive title\par
   - Select appropriate type\par
   - Define clear steps\par
   - Specify expected results\par
   - Link to story\par
\par
\tab 3. **Review Test Case**\par
   - Peer review for completeness\par
   - Validate against criteria\par
   - Ensure reproducibility\par
\par
\tab 4. **Execute Test**\par
   - Follow steps exactly\par
   - Record actual results\par
   - Note any deviations\par
   - Report bugs if needed\par
\par
\tab 5. **Maintain Tests**\par
   - Update when requirements change\par
   - Retire obsolete tests\par
   - Refactor for clarity\par
\par
\fs28\b Bug Reporting Workflow\b0\fs22\par
\par
\tab 1. **Discover Bug**\par
   - During test execution or ad-hoc testing\par
   - Document immediately\par
\par
\tab 2. **Report Bug**\par
   - Clear, specific title\par
   - Detailed description\par
   - Exact reproduction steps\par
   - Expected vs actual behavior\par
   - Environment details\par
   - Screenshots/logs\par
\par
\tab 3. **Triage**\par
   - Assign severity\par
   - Link to story\par
   - Assign to developer\par
   - Set priority\par
\par
\tab 4. **Development**\par
   - Developer reproduces\par
   - Fixes issue\par
   - Updates status to "Fixed"\par
   - Links commit\par
\par
\tab 5. **Verification**\par
   - Tester re-executes test\par
   - Confirms fix\par
   - Marks "Verified"\par
\par
\tab 6. **Closure**\par
   - Final review\par
   - Mark "Closed"\par
   - Document in release notes\par
\par
\fs28\b Sprint Planning Workflow\b0\fs22\par
\par
\tab 1. **Pre-Planning**\par
   - Review backlog\par
   - Groom stories\par
   - Estimate story points\par
\par
\tab 2. **Sprint Creation**\par
   - Create sprint\par
   - Set goal and dates\par
   - Set team capacity\par
\par
\tab 3. **Story Selection**\par
   - Choose high-priority stories\par
   - Ensure total points ≤ capacity\par
   - Verify all stories approved\par
\par
\tab 4. **Test Planning**\par
   - Review AI test recommendations\par
   - Create necessary test cases\par
   - Assign testers\par
\par
\tab 5. **Sprint Execution**\par
   - Daily standup\par
   - Update progress\par
   - Monitor burndown\par
\par
\tab 6. **Sprint Closure**\par
   - Complete remaining tests\par
   - Verify all done items\par
   - Generate sprint report\par
   - Hold retrospective\par
