\fs32\b Glossary\b0\fs22\par\par
\par
\\b Acceptance Criteria\\b0 - Specific conditions that must be met for a story to be considered complete\par
\par
\\b Burn-Down Chart\\b0 - Graph showing work remaining over time\par
\par
\\b Coverage\\b0 - Percentage of requirements/code that have tests\par
\par
\\b Defect Density\\b0 - Number of bugs per module or per line of code\par
\par
\\b KPI\\b0 - Key Performance Indicator, measurable value showing effectiveness\par
\par
\\b QA Sign-Off\\b0 - QA engineer approval that acceptance criteria are testable\par
\par
\\b PM Approval\\b0 - Product manager approval that story is ready for development\par
\par
\\b Regression Test\\b0 - Test to ensure previously working functionality still works\par
\par
\\b Risk Level\\b0 - Assessment of potential impact and likelihood of issues\par
\par
\\b Severity\\b0 - Degree of impact a bug has on the system\par
\par
\\b Smoke Test\\b0 - Basic test to verify critical functionality works\par
\par
\\b Sprint\\b0 - Fixed time period (usually 2 weeks) for completing work\par
\par
\\b Story Points\\b0 - Relative measure of effort/complexity\par
\par
\\b Traceability\\b0 - Ability to link requirements to tests to bugs\par
\par
\\b Velocity\\b0 - Amount of work completed in a sprint\par
\par
